{
  "description": "Issue #1025 Part B (decline B2 from #1021): `( foo.bar )` reading as a `parenthesized-call` with a stray `.` -- `.` is not infix, so the pre-existing one-token lookahead never saw it -- is FIXED rather than recorded as a limitation. Before the fix `print ( origin.x )` raised `ol-bad-token` at parse while the bare `print origin.x` parsed clean; here both read the struct field and print 7, so this asserts the READ agrees, not merely that both spellings are quiet. The `.field` half of the postfix lookahead deliberately needs NO adjacency, matching `collectPostfixSegments`, so `( origin . x )` agrees too; that spelling and the newline one (`spec/grammar.md:34` makes newlines insignificant inside one group) are pinned as unit tests in `packages/parser/src/multiline-expressions.test.mjs`. The returned record carries the reserved `__type` opt-in, so the fixture pins the struct type and not just the field values.",
